Junior doctors plan to launch further strike after rejecting Jeremy Hunt's proposal
The ministers initially hoped to end the change-induced dispute by accepting a contract amended by British Medical Association (BMA) officials, but 58 per cent of the 37,000 junior doctors who participated in the vote objected to the contract.
