Primark customers angry at a woman who brazenly tried on panties in the middle of the store
A woman undresses on the spot in the middle of a Primark store, and the customers in the store don’t know where to look.
To make matters worse, she also looked at what she looked like when she put it on, then took off her underwear and put it back on the shelf.
She continued to browse the shelves and eventually tried out four panties at the Bouverie Place shopping mall in Folkestone.
The woman continued to try on panties in this Primark store at the Bouverie Place shopping mall in Folkestone before putting it back on the shelves.
Jenny Davidson (the mother of the two children), who was also in the store at the time, said that after trying on the underwear, the mysterious woman "dressed again and then walked out of the store and didn't buy anything."
“Everyone can’t believe what they’ve seen.”
She stood in the middle of the shop, took a pair of panties from the shelf, took off her leggings and panties, and put them on.
“She didn’t try to find a hidden place—she just stood there, it’s impudent.”
“When she took off her panties again, they were all dumbfounded. Obviously, she wasn’t happy because she put them back on the shelf.”
Later, she tried three times like this, and finally found that she did not like it, and then got dressed again and went out of the store.
“She didn’t seem to care if someone was looking at her—or she didn’t even think anyone was going to end up buying the underwear she’d tried.”
Ms. Davidson, a 33-year-old who lives in the town of Kent, said: “It’s disgusting to think that someone would buy panties that other people wear and haven’t washed.”
It happened on Tuesday afternoon.
Ms. Davidson added: “After she left, it became clear that the shopkeeper was going to take these panties off the shelves, fortunately.”
“I hate to go home with a new pair of trousers, only to find that another woman has tried and hasn’t been cleaned.”
A spokesperson for Primark said: “Primark is aware of what happened at our Folkestone store on Tuesday, Aug. 9.
All the goods in question have been removed.
