Non-Beijing citizens who have lived in Beijing for more than 6 months and meet one of the conditions of legal and stable employment, legal and stable residence and continuous study in Beijing can apply for a residence permit.
Recently, the implementation rules of Beijing's "provisional regulations on residence permits" have been issued, which means that the "temporary residence permit" will be upgraded to a "residency permit".
The person in charge of the relevant departments said that the change from "temporary residence permit" to "residual residence permit" means that Beijing's non-Beijing resident population will shift from "management" to multi-faceted services.
