A third-party (non-Chinese company) commissioned by the Olympic Organizing Committee to produce the national flag is located in the Brazilian state of São Paulo, about 75 kilometers from the city of São Paulo.
In order to urge the manufacturers to be completed as soon as possible, the Chinese Consulate General in Sao Paulo organized special personnel to go to the manufacturers to do in-depth work.
After more than 30 hours of overtime, the manufacturer has finally completed the production of the Chinese flag and loaded the car, and the task that originally required 4-5 working days was completed in advance.
It is reported that the national flag is expected to arrive in Rio on the 11th, and the Olympic Organizing Committee will be sent to various Olympic venues after receiving the flag, and the whole process will be completed under the supervision of Chinese embassies and consulates in Brazil.
On the 10th, the Nantong municipal government held the Hutong industrial cooperation talks event at the Shanghai International Convention Center, and more than 180 Shanghai enterprises were invited to participate, and more than 20 billion yuan of Hutong industrial docking projects were signed on the spot.
With a total investment of 8.063 billion yuan in 20 projects signed, it covers many industries such as new energy, new materials and modern service industries.
Qingdao is the country's 12th and the country's first pilot city for the paid use and trading of pollutant rights in Shandong Province.
On the 11th, a large number of enterprises came to the Qingdao sewage rights trading center to submit the requisition of sewage rights, after the requisition will pay a paid use fee.
The soon-to-be-completed first order of the transaction also indicates that the pilot work of Qingdao's sewage rights transaction has officially kicked off, which will also be the first list of the province's sewage rights transaction and the first order of the national urban-level sewage rights transaction.
On the morning of the 11th, Zhao Xiuping, general manager of Qingdao Shuangtao Fine Chemical (Group) Co., Ltd., came to the Qingdao sewage rights trading center to submit the requisition of sewage rights.
At the end of last year, the company's factory in the old town of Qingdao was completely shut down, and the environmental protection was relocated to the new factory in Pingdu.
After Zhao Xiuping submitted materials such as application forms and environmental impact reports for construction projects, the Qingdao sewage rights reserve and trading service center began a preliminary examination of the application materials.
According to the collection standards determined by the price, finance and other departments in Qingdao, the current pre-anticipated initial sewage rights use fee is about 641,200 yuan, and the staff will complete the approval within 7 working days.
The soon-to-be-completed first order of the transaction also indicates that the pilot work of Qingdao's sewage rights transaction has officially begun, and it will also be the first order of the province's sewage rights transaction and the first order of the country's municipal-level sewage rights transaction.
Zhao Xiuping said that at present, the environmental protection of enterprises has invested up to 400 million, on the surface of a huge amount, but it has a great impact on enterprise management concepts and social benefits, and it has also opened up space for enterprise innovation and management.
On the same day, Qingdao Sifang Xincheng Zhizhuo Bus Accessories Co., Ltd. also applied for sewage rights for an annual output of 4,200 high-speed rail and EMU interior accessories projects.
The project belongs to the mechanical processing enterprises, and the initial sewage rights applied for are chemical oxygen demand (COD) 0.514 tons / year, ammonia nitrogen (NOX) 0.052 tons / year.
Atmospheric pollutant discharge rights are used and traded for the city's key industrial enterprises for the supply of electricity and heat.
By January 1, 2016, the existing polluting units that have obtained the environmental impact assessment will not be levied on paid royalties.
“Reimbursement of the right to discharge pollution does not amount to obtaining the power of illegal sewage discharge, and it is not possible to discharge pollutants at will.”
Han Hongyan, deputy director of the Qingdao Municipal Environmental Protection Bureau, said that if the illegal discharge of pollution and excessive sewage should still be punished in accordance with the relevant laws and regulations, it is impossible to allow illegal enterprises to circumvent the punishment through the purchase of sewage rights.
In other words, through legal means to severely crack down on environmental violations and severely punish enterprises for excessive polluting behavior, so as to protect the environment and protect public health.
At present, for its own interests, enterprises have improved the enthusiasm for pollution control, cherished the limited emission rights, and reduced pollutant emissions.
Driven by economic interests, reducing pollutant emissions has changed from the government's compulsory behavior to the conscious market behavior of enterprises, so as to truly achieve the purpose of protecting the environment, protecting nature and protecting public health.
The right to discharge pollution, also known as "emission right", is the right to discharge pollutants, and refers to the right to discharge pollutants into the environment according to law, within the amount allocated by the government.
In essence, this right is the right of polluters to possess, use, and benefit from environmental capacity resources.
In the next step, under the premise that the total pollutant discharge does not exceed the allowable emissions, the internal pollutant sources will adjust each other through currency exchange.
