On February 22 this year, the United States and Russia reached an agreement on the ceasefire between the parties to the conflict in Syria, and the ceasefire agreement began to be implemented on the 27th of the same month.
According to the agreement, the ceasefire does not include military strikes against terrorist organizations identified by the United Nations Security Council, such as the Islamic State "Support Front".
Russia will continue to build the relevant military infrastructure at the base, and the living conditions of Russian military personnel will also be correspondingly guaranteed.
He also said that if the extremist forces are not attacked, these forces will be extended to Russia.
Although Russia and the West have not reached an agreement to jointly combat extremist forces in Syria, Russia will strengthen cooperation with Syria, Iran and Iraq in this regard.
In September 2015, at the invitation of the Syrian government, Russia began to carry out military strikes against extremist forces in Syria.
On March 15 of this year, the main Russian military forces stationed in Syria began to withdraw, but the Russian side promised to continue to maintain the Khmeimim air base and the Tartus naval base.
