The traffic control department of Songjiang District in Shanghai recently used electronic police to remediate the driver's car to play with his mobile phone and seized more than 30 cases in a week.
With the popularization of smart phones, mobile phones are becoming more and more fun, brushing WeChat, micro-blogging and even playing games and visiting Taobao has become the norm, and many people seem to be inseparable from their mobile phones, and they can't even stop when driving.
The Road Traffic Safety Act explicitly forbids the use of mobile phones and defines it as an “obstruction of safe driving behavior”.
Regrettably, this phenomenon has not been duly punished for reasons such as the number of violators and the difficulty of obtaining evidence, and the provisions of the law have almost become furnishings.
If the traffic control department can be determined to "declaration of war" on the act of driving and playing with mobile phones and normalize this measure, this illegal behavior will surely be curbed.
