In the collective greenhouse of Donglin Village in Taicang City, 48-year-old Wang Xuefen is taking workers to spray pear trees with pesticides.
There are more than 150 acres of orchards and more than 10 tree species in the whole village, which requires only 12 workers plus 1 technical engineer.
A total of 50,000 yuan last year, like my age, if you work in the factory will certainly not get this money.
Last year, Donglin village income reached 22 million yuan, of which total agricultural income accounted for nearly half.
The per capita land planting area is increasing every year, starting with 50 acres, and now more than 100 acres; the efficiency of each mu is increasing every year, and the income of professional farmers is also increasing every year.
Judging the shares to every villager, the biggest highlight of the collective economic reform of rural areas is to clarify the property rights of rural collective operating assets and explore the separation of politics and economy.
In July 2015, 14 rural economic cooperation organizations and their village committees were "segmented account management" in Anzhen Street in Xishan District of Wuxi City, and the village committee carried out the management of rural public affairs, and the cooperative organizations were mainly engaged in operations.
There are two accounts between the two institutions, which do not "break the border" with each other to prevent village cadres from participating in collective asset management.
Zhu Bao Ping, deputy director of the Jiangsu Provincial Agricultural Committee, said that Jiangsu will continue to promote the reform of the community joint-stock cooperation system in the next step, encourage the joint development of farmers, and establish a mechanism for the operation of democratic power at the village level.
Zhu Baoping: further promote the reform, engage in community-share cooperation, quantification of assets to members, fixed to farmers, the formation of clear property rights.
Through the Internet +, the implementation of his right to information, the right to participate in decision-making and the supervision of democratic management, the implementation of the three rights to the farmers, and indeed make it into a standardized operation mechanism for joint-stock cooperation.
At present, the new collective economy of southern rural areas has mainly formed four development models of asset leasing, enterprise shares, agricultural development and joint development.
