The British "Guardian" commented that the symbolic representation of Switzerland, a neutral country, played a role in the British prime minister's choice of the first resort.
The British "Daily Telegraph" commented that Theresa May chose to go to Switzerland for a vacation, which is the first time that the British Prime Minister went to Switzerland after Margaret Thatcher.
There is a contrast between the choices of the two female prime ministers and the two male prime ministers of Blair and Cameron like to travel to hotter places.
Britain’s new prime minister, Theresa May, will return to London on August 24 with a series of important work and activities waiting for her.
Britain’s parliament is set to reconvene on Sept. 5, with a debate focused on online calls for a second Brexit referendum.
On June 23, the United Kingdom decided to leave the EU in a referendum, but the new British Prime Minister is not willing to launch the content of Article 50 of the Lisbon Treaty related to the withdrawal of member states by the end of the year.
