China's Mars program has arrived.
China's Mars exploration mission to achieve encircling, landing and patrolling at a time, this form has never been seen in foreign countries.
China's Mars exploration and launch goal is to surround, land and patrol in one step, and this mission has considerable difficulty.
Because it will take 26 months for the Mars exploration to encounter a time window, the experts are closely developing an engineering plan to launch China's first Mars probe in this window in 2020.
Although China's vehicles have entered deep space, it is still indispensable to complete the Mars exploration mission, which means that China has entered the era of deep space exploration in a real sense.
“Every two or three years, there is an opportunity for Mars to be closest to the Earth, at this point in time to launch a Mars probe, which is the most energy-efficient for the launch vehicle.”
“In view of the quality of the Mars probe, the launch mission will be carried out by China's Long March 5 launch vehicle.”
China's Mars exploration mission to achieve encircling, landing, inspection, this form has never happened in foreign countries, abroad has planned to achieve circumnavigation and landing, but the landing failed.
There are a lot of technical fields involved in the exploration of Mars, in particular, although the rover is a space probe, it has distinctive characteristics compared with ordinary space probes.
In other words, the Mars probe must have the ability to determine the driving route and detect the danger of obstacles.
Pang Zhihao, a researcher at the Fifth Academy of the China Aerospace Science and Technology Group, said that the reason why human beings are so favored for Mars exploration is that it has important scientific and technological significance, and it is even related to the future of mankind.
At present, Mars has become the planet with the highest degree of human research in addition to Earth, and the history of human use of space probes to carry out Mars exploration almost throughout the entire history of human spaceflight.
Therefore, human beings hope to one day establish a habitation base on Mars, and eventually migrate to Mars and turn it into a second home for human beings.
There are also plenty of indications that Mars is likely to be the same as the current Earth, only after billions of years of evolution to become a thin atmosphere, low temperature, water depletion and so on.
Therefore, the exploration or manned landing on Mars for research can put forward a plan to prevent the earth from becoming the second Mars that is difficult for humans to survive.
As of June 2016, there have been a total of 114 lunar probes and forty-three Mars explorations worldwide.
However, since the 1990s, humans have carried out a total of 18 Mars explorations, while only 14 lunar explorations have been carried out.
At present, there are five Mars orbiters and two Mars rovers in operation, but only one lunar orbiter and one lunar lander are in operation.
The world's major space powers have developed exploration plans aimed at the Mars system, so it can be seen that today's Mars exploration is hotter than lunar exploration.
On November 5, 2013, India launched its first Mars probe "Mangarian", becoming the first country in Asia to successfully explore Mars.
"Mangarian" is used to study the surface, atmosphere and mineral characteristics of Mars to see whether there are signs of methane and life on Mars.
The most difficult part of this mission is the pneumatic shape and parachute deceleration after the probe enters the atmosphere of Mars with only one chance.
According to Sun Zezhou, the chief designer of the Mars probe in the overall department of China Aerospace Science and Technology Group Corporation, Mars exploration missions face many technical challenges.
The atmospheric pressure of Mars is very low, only 1% of the atmospheric pressure of the Earth's surface, which has a very high degree of uncertainty.
Scientists do not yet have a thorough understanding of factors such as its changes and the nature of the storm.
In the summer, Mars will often form dust storms similar to Earth's dust weather, which will lead to a sharp decline in the solar energy received by the rover, and it must design a "dormant" mode for the rover to patiently wait for the dust storm to pass.
At the same time, the atmosphere of Mars also has a reduced effect on the sun's light, which poses a problem for the energy supply of Mars exploration.
This means that the probe's solar wing area is larger, and it needs to be constantly adjusted and strives to be aimed in the direction of the sun.
In addition, the gravity on the surface of Mars is only 38% that of the Earth, but it is much larger than the gravity on the lunar surface, so the probe needs more power.
“The most central and most difficult part of this Mars exploration mission is the pneumatic shape and parachute deceleration after the probe enters the Martian atmosphere, and there is only one chance to ensure success.”
Sun Zezhou said that due to the distance between the earth and Mars, the whole process can not be controlled by the ground in real time, so it must be completed independently by the probe.
Because there are not so many propellants to offset such a high velocity, the deceleration depends on the role of the Martian atmosphere when landing on Mars, which is difficult to simulate on the ground.
Pang Zhihao said that in general, the method of detecting Mars is similar to that of exploring the moon, and it is also "circling, landing, patrolling and returning", and finally achieving the goal of manned landing on Mars.
Because Mars is much farther from the Earth than the Moon, it is necessary to overcome a series of more complex technical difficulties.
According to Taiwan's media reports, Taiwan's "administrative president" Lin Quan announced yesterday morning that the "Regulations on the improper acquisition of property by political parties and their affiliated organizations" came into effect from today.
Zhan Qixian, vice chairman of the Kuomintang, said: "A more than 100-year-old Kuomintang, with social commitments and responsibilities, will not collapse in this way."
Lin Quan stressed that if political parties, affiliated organizations or trustees violate the prohibition of sanctions stipulated in the regulations, the committee will investigate them according to their authority and "in accordance with the law".
Lin Quan also announced that he should not be the vice chairman of the party's production committee, and Hong Bacon, the "deputy director" of Taiwan's ICAC, will serve.
Gu Lixiong as the main committee of the improper party property committee is not the same candidate, borrowing Hong Bacon's experience in investigating relevant major cases in the past will be used as the basis for the committee to inventory related improper party property cases.
Zhan Qixian believes that today, as long as there are party property, no one will give you social donations, if the party's property system is confiscated, the Kuomintang can just ask for social support and sponsorship, "today there is really no opportunity to go."
Zhan Qixian also stressed that even after the party's property regulations are on the road, the Kuomintang's property has not been completely confiscated and confiscated, and the rest will still be donated according to the promise, so that the party's property will go to zero, and the party wants everything to start from scratch.
The original title: "the corridor doctor" Lan Yuefeng v. CCTV host Wang Zhi'an's reputation infringement lost the first-instance lawsuit
Legal Evening News because CCTV moderator Wang Zhi'an published remarks on Sina Weibo about the "colonial doctor" incident, Lan Yuefeng sued Wang Zhi'an and Beijing Weimeng Chuangke Network Technology Co., Ltd. to the court.
In the afternoon of yesterday, the Haidian court issued a judgment on the case, and the judgment found that Wang Zhi'an and Wei Meng Company did not constitute infringement, and rejected all the claims of Lan Yuefeng.
At the beginning of 2014, CCTV reporter Wang Zhi'an's investigation found that although Lan Yuefeng, who sat in the hospital corridor for more than 600 days, had been portrayed by the media as a tragic hero who had been suppressed by the system, there was a large amount of false information in these reports.
On March 29, 2014, the "Clarity Doctor" program produced by CCTV News was broadcast.
All kinds of so-called excessive medical information reported by Lan Yuefeng to the media are not supported by evidence.
Wang Zhi'an is also in the real-name certified micro-blog, describing that "the reason why Lan Yuefeng came to this step is because of personality, with its obvious paranoid personality and so on."
Lan Yuefeng asked Wang Zhi'an to delete the micro-blog, apologizing to him and compensating 100,000 yuan for moral damages.
At the trial at that time, the two sides debated whether Wang Zhi'an had infringed Lan Yuefeng's reputational rights.
