Since the suspect is a frequent offender of theft, he has been repeatedly cracked down by the public security organs, has a strong anti-reconnaissance ability, coupled with his long-term use of drugs, interrogation addiction often occurs, interrogation work is very difficult.
The Greenland shark, also known as the small-headed sleeping shark, is widely distributed in the waters of the North Atlantic Ocean around Greenland and Iceland, reaching a height of 4 to 5 meters in adulthood.
However, their growth rate is extremely slow, sometimes only about one centimeter a year long, which suggests that Greenland sharks may have the life of a foreign minister.
Traditional chronometric methods often use animal calcified tissues, and fin ridges can be used in some sharks, but such calcified tissue is very rare in Greenland sharks.
The new study, led by Julius Nelson at the University of Copenhagen in Denmark, turns to radiocarbon dating using the eye lens of a Greenland shark.
This method has previously been used to determine the age of whales, but for the first time, it has been used to determine the age of fish such as sharks.
According to their analysis, the largest shark has an estimated life expectancy of 392 years, with an error of 120 years.
In other words, this shark is at least 272 years old and may be as high as 512 years old.
In addition, it is said that female Greenland sharks can only become sexually mature until they are about 4 meters long, which translates to at least 156 years of age.
As a result, the researchers wrote in the paper that Greenland sharks are the oldest known vertebrates on the planet, surpassing previous long-lived champion circuit whales (211 years old).
Over the past year, the exchange rate has achieved remarkable results, the RMB exchange rate has remained basically stable, and it has also laid the foundation for promoting the internationalization of the RMB.
Judging from the performance of the market, in the past year, the two-way fluctuation characteristics of the RMB exchange rate have been obvious, the exchange rate flexibility has increased, and the exchange rate is expected to be generally stable.
The exchange rate has changed so far, and the fluctuation of the middle price of the RMB against the U.S. dollar has repeatedly appeared, but the process has alternated.
Last year's "8.11" exchange rate reform before the implementation of last year's "8.11" exchange reform measures was implemented in 2005, and the RMB appreciated significantly against the United States dollar in the past decade.
Since the implementation of the new foreign exchange rate reform, the RMB has changed its previous state of appreciation, and the middle price of the RMB exchange rate has depreciated by about 8% in the past year.
On October 1 this year, the International Monetary Fund will officially accept the RMB and become the weighted currency of the SDR (Special Drawing Rights).
According to statistics released by the General Administration of Customs this week, in the first seven months of this year, the total value of China's imports and exports was 13.21 trillion yuan, a decrease of 3% compared with the same period last year.
In the same month of July, the total value of China's imports and exports fell by only 0.9% year-on-year, especially the year-on-year increase in exports by 2.9%.
Relevant experts believe that although imports and exports showed signs of stabilising in July, they should not be too high expectations.
In July, the total value of China's imports and exports was 2.09 trillion yuan, down 0.9% year-on-year.
Among them, exports 1.22 trillion yuan, an increase of 2.9%; imports of 873 billion yuan, down 5.7%; trade surplus of 342.8 billion yuan, an increase of 34%.
Although the total value of imports and exports still fell year-on-year, there was an increase in export data, which is the fifth consecutive monthly increase in exports since March this year.
More than 3,400 people in four months, Shanghai police cracked down on 157 "stealing and cheating" gangs.
At the same time as the detection of the case, the police also recovered a total of more than 33 million yuan.
According to the statement of the members of the theft gang, they entered Shanghai from the field by chartered black car, and then got out of the car separately, a few hours later, they would close the car and then leave Shanghai together.
In the course of the crime, the criminal suspects often use a building as a unit, using the external wall to climb and break the anti-theft window fencing from the top to the "sweeping" theft from top to bottom.
A few days ago, the criminal suspects involved in the case have been transferred to the Xuhui District Procuratorate for review and prosecution.
The police remind the general public that they must lock the doors and windows in their homes when they go out, and it is recommended that the public should choose steel with a harder material for anti-theft windows.
In late August, Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe will go to Kenya to attend the 6th African Development Conference.
The African development conference is led by Japan, and the previous five meetings were held in Tokyo or Yokohama, Japan, so the meeting will also be the first to move to Africa.
Japan's Foreign Ministry official said that the local meeting in Africa will help attract the attention of African and European countries to Japan.
In order to cooperate with Abe's foreign visit, according to Kyodo News, the Liberal Democratic Party of Japan will send parliamentarians to the relevant countries.
It’s no coincidence that Japan’s road to “normalization” began in the early 1990’s, and it’s no coincidence that the Japan-initiated Africa Development Conference also began in 1993!
Africa has 53 seats in the United Nations, is an important ticket warehouse of the United Nations, if Japan wants to "regular", how to abandon Africa?
It will also exchange views with relevant people from various countries on the extremist organization "Islamic State" and countermeasures for terrorist activities.
The “Western Group” will visit seven countries, including Sierra Leone, Liberia and Guinea-Bissau.
Japanese Foreign Minister Fumio Kishio Kishida also recently explained his intentions for the African development meeting at the United Nations Security Council.
Abe announced here that for the stability of sub-Saharan African countries, it will provide 100 billion yen (about 6.1 billion yuan) of assistance within five years.
Observers generally believe that Japan's generosity to Africa has always had two main purposes: one is to increase Japan's sense of presence in Africa; the other is to win the support of African countries on the issue.
Yang Bojiang, an expert on Japan, said: “From a political point of view, although the relative development of Africa lags behind, the number of countries is relatively large, so Japan has always regarded it as the so-called ‘big ticket field’.”
In the future, Japan will not give up, and the work for Africa will not be terminated and will be continuously strengthened.
In terms of the economy, because Japan's production capacity is relatively strong, but the domestic market is relatively limited, especially at present, in the context of the aging of young children, domestic demand is relatively sluggish.
However, from Junichiro Koizumi 10 years ago, to Abe 10 years later, during this period, Japan has repeatedly launched a "sprint", but they all returned.
Yang Bojiang, an expert on the issue of Japan, believes that Japan's usual intention is obvious at a glance, but it is bound to be difficult.
In order to achieve its own goals, Japan must first have good relations with neighboring countries, among which Japan needs to have a correct attitude on the issue of geopolitics and ethnic disputes and historical understanding.
The Haikou Maritime Court filed a case in the early morning to ensure the rights and interests of the parties involved in the sinking of the Lingao fishing boat.
The relatives of the three dead crew members rushed to the Haikou Maritime Court at 4 a.m. on August 7 to pre-indict an application for property preservation and seizure of the suspected freighter.
After the incident on the 4th, the suspected freighter was detained by the Maritime Affairs Bureau to assist in the investigation.
In view of the fact that the 72-hour detention period of the Maritime Affairs Bureau expired at 9 a.m. on August 7, the relatives of the victims filed a property preservation application with the court in the early morning of August 7.
At 4:20 o'clock in the morning, the applicant's property preservation before the lawsuit was filed, and the on-duty marshal was patiently received.
