Traditional customs introduce a new bright spot "2016 Yulan Cultural Festival" Hong Kong Victoria Park opened
The music of drumming, traditional snacks, fancy decorations, and the raging scene of the crowd.
Hosted by the Hong Kong Twilight Society Association, the "2016 Bolan Cultural Festival" was held in Victoria Park from the 12th to the 14th, which is Hong Kong's largest event.
In addition to the continuation of the existing "orphan competition", it has also increased the "parent-child basin stacking competition" that the whole family can participate in.
It not only uses comic forms to introduce the culture and history, but also has a Bolan-themed 3D selfie area, a traditional snack area, and a traditional craft mobile classroom, which attracts a lot of children and overseas people to experience the visit.
A couple from France lingered for nearly three hours at the event site and experienced it in a mini-card mobile classroom.
"I found this special festival online, so I decided to take a look and it's very fresh."
They pointed out that although France also has similar festivals to commemorate the ancestors, the atmosphere is very heavy, unlike here, there is music, there is food can also learn traditional craftsmanship.
She said, "In such a busy financial metropolis in Hong Kong, we can also see such a large-scale and organized ceremony to worship our ancestors."
"This not only reflects the diversity of Chinese culture, but also allows more people to learn about these traditional craftsmanship and pass it on."
At the event, the president of the event, Hu Yansong, said: “We do not want to make the festival so horrific that it does not allow people to approach them, especially children.”
"We hope that through the rejuvenation activities and layout of the scene, let young people know that what is filial piety and gratitude want to be expressed behind the festival culture."
He also pointed out that a total of 24 teams participated in the "orientation competition", which not only has community organizations, but also cooperates with some schools to allow students to participate.
It is understood that in 2011, the Hong Kong Trenzi Lansheng Association has been included in the "National Intangible Cultural Heritage List" in 2011.
On the evening of the 11th, China's National Peking Theatre took the famous drama "White Snake" through thousands of miles to come to Mexico City and presented an authentic Beijing opera feast for the local people at the Mexican National Palace of Fine Arts.
From August 9th to 23rd, from August 9th to 23rd, the Chinese National Peking Theatre performed 7 Peking operas in Mexico City, the capital of Mexico, as well as five cities such as Cordoba and Juárez.
Spectators follow the "White Snake" plot, the actor's singing and playing, sometimes smiling, and sometimes warmly applause.
Marissa Jimenez Cacho, who had watched Peking Opera 15 years ago, accompanied her daughter to the show.
"It's a wonderful performance, the music, the lighting, the stage performance I'm very impressed... I think it's very necessary to let my daughter also learn about Chinese culture and Chinese Peking opera art."
The enthusiasm of the Mexican audience left a deep impression on the white lady's protagonist and the young actors.
“I didn’t expect the Mexican audience to be so enthusiastic, and I was a little worried about their ability to understand the story, but it came to my surprise today to see that they could capture the storyline and so many laughs.”
Qiu Xiaoqi, Chinese Ambassador to Mexico, said that the cultural exchange activities of this year's Sino-Ukrainian Cultural Exchange have played a positive role in promoting deeper understanding and enhancing friendship between the two peoples.
Next year will mark the 45th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries, during which there will be more cultural exchange activities between the two countries.
Liu Yigui went to Sanya to investigate the "double repair, two cities" requirements to improve the level of urban construction and management
