The biggest advantage of VR works is that the audience has a unique "immersion", which also puts forward higher requirements for the filming process.
The filming team of the "Polar" panoramic VR special edition said that they want to make sure that the picture in every direction is impeccable, so that the audience has an immersive feeling.
On August 11, the Yantai detachment of the Shandong Armed Police Corps organized special combat snipers to come to the jungle to carry out jungle training in Quncao Mountain with a high temperature of 34 degrees Celsius.
During the Cold War, the Soviet Union brought missiles into Cuba, which almost led to a nuclear war between the United States and the Soviet Union.
This incident is regarded as the culmination of the Cold War, known as the "Cuban Missile Crisis".
What is less well known, however, was that during the Cold War, a strong solar storm nearly led the United States to launch a nuclear war against the Soviet Union, an event that was not first announced by researchers until Aug. 9.
On May 23, 1967, a strong solar storm caused intense interference with the U.S. military’s radar and radio communications in the Arctic.
The radars are part of a U.S. ballistic missile early warning system used to monitor Soviet missiles.
The paper, completed by researchers at the University of Colorado, interviewed U.S. military personnel who were involved in forecasting and analyzing solar activity at that time, and looked at unconfided literature.
In the 1960s, in order to prevent a sudden nuclear war by the Soviet Union, the U.S. Air Force always had a number of warplanes loaded with nuclear warheads flying into the sky.
The U.S. military commander did not know that the main cause of the interference was the solar storm, not the Soviet Union, so he ordered the fighters into combat readiness.
Fortunately, the U.S. U.S. military’s study of solar activity and its electromagnetic interference on the Earth, which began in the late 1950s, eventually prevented this potential military conflict.
Later, he aggregated the information provided by the U.S. Air Force’s Aeronautical Meteorology Service and submitted a detailed report.
As a direct result of this solar storm, the U.S. military began to view space weather as an operational concern and established a more robust space weather forecasting system.
In the daily travel of the public, it is found that the love car is hindered by strange vehicles, in the absence of unfamiliar vehicle drivers, you can use the "WeChat mobile car" function to solve this problem.
Since August 11th, Xi'an traffic police WeChat service number "Xi Xi'an traffic police" launched "WeChat mobile car" service.
After the launch of this service, citizens can solve such problems through the use of the "WeChat mobile car" function in the case of unfamiliar vehicles when the driver is not on the scene.
This new service function is fast to save administrative costs; the second is to respect and protect the personal privacy of citizens; the third is to provide round-the-clock and full-time services.
As long as the public has WeChat, they can operate on their own in a very convenient way, this method can make both sides of the car relatively friendly and easy to "meet", to alleviate the problem of parking difficulties, and to reduce the occurrence of car-related public security cases.
On the other hand, for car owners who refuse to move their cars, illegally park or obstruct traffic, the Xi'an traffic control department said that the traffic police will take different disposal measures according to the actual situation at that time and deal with them according to the situation.
