On April 27, 2015, the United States and Japan jointly released a new version of the U.S.-Japan defense cooperation guidelines in New York, allowing the Japanese armed forces to play a more offensive role around the world.
On the same day, U.S. Defense Secretary Carter, U.S. Secretary of State Kerry, Japanese Foreign Minister Kishio Kishida and Japanese Defense Minister Nakamura attended a press conference in New York.
This is the fifth time that a Chinese private think tank has published Japan's military force assessment report, and it is also the fourth time that the English version has been
The report is divided into nine chapters, including overall policy adjustment, military strength, national defense budget, military deployment, weapons and equipment, institutional reform, military training exercises, foreign military security cooperation, and military security relations with China.
According to the report, 2015 marks the end of several consecutive years of major policy adjustments by the Abe government in the field of security.
Since then, Japan's measures in the field of security will mainly focus on operational aspects such as the application of the rule of law, strategic implementation and policy implementation, rather than substantial adjustments and changes in frameworks, mechanisms and policies.
According to the report, Abe's cabinet is trying to achieve the multiple purposes of promoting Japan's "normal nationalization", self-Defense forces going out and intervening in international security affairs, strengthening the Japan-U.S.-US alliance, and strengthening the Japan-U.S. alliance.
Previously, the China Association for the Promotion of Strategic and Cultural Affairs released the Japanese military assessment report on June 5, 2012, July 19, 2013, July 23, 2014, and June 30, 2015.
On August 12, the Financial Times released an atlas of a set of U.S. ambassador’s residences in China.
In contrast, the U.S. ambassador’s official residence, in terms of its appearance, can be used as a safe house in the next film adapted from John Le Carrey’s Cold War spy novels.
The official residence is gray and is heavily guarded with perimeter guardrails, a second inner wall, barbed-wire and vehicle barricades.
Compulsory public sports facilities
The black coal yard warehouse has become a "green grass" football field; the red-brick spire factory has become a modern sports hall.
On the national fitness day, the South Lok Ma camp sports and cultural park outside the Wangjiang Gate in Hangzhou unveiled the mysterious veil.
It used to be a coal farm and has been idle since it was closed more than a decade ago, leaving behind a large number of illegal buildings and domestic waste.
After rectification, it has become a sports and cultural park, and will be officially opened to the public in November, providing free sports venues to the public, which will undoubtedly open up a new fertile ground for national sports.
This can't help but remind people of the Hangzhou Chen Jinglong Sports School, China's "Wangpu Military Academy", which has swam a number of world championships.
There will be a steady stream of names for swimming, vividly exemplifiing the relationship between competitive sports and national sports – a rich mass base that provides good conditions for the selection of professional players.
The level of competitive sports is closely related to the foundation of national sports, competitive sports in a certain sense depends on national sports, and national sports depends on venue conditions.
According to reports, as of 2015, although China's per capita stadium area has been 150 times that of the founding of New China, it is still far behind the sports powers.
In June of this year, the State Council issued the National Fitness Plan (2016-2020), which took the development of people's sports as a key content.
In order to complete this short board, on the one hand, the relevant departments should fully take into account the layout of sports venues when carrying out urban planning.
On the other hand, public sports stadiums that have been built, including sports stadiums in schools and other units, should expand the scope of openness as much as possible and improve the efficiency of their use as much as possible.
At present, the Rio Olympic Games, which is in full swing, has stimulated people's enthusiasm for sports and awakened everyone's sense of participation.
Gilead gets lawyer's fees in battle with Merck's hepatitis C patents
According to the U.S. district judge’s decision, Gilead Sciences is entitled to attorney’s fees incurred in a hepatitis C patent lawsuit with the U.S. Merck Group.
In June, after a U.S. judge found Merck’s violations, including perjury and other unethical behavior, Gilead avoided paying $200 million in damages resulting from Gilead’s best-selling Sofosbuvir and Havalney infringing on two of Merck’s patents.
In Thursday’s lawsuit, U.S. District Judge Beth Ramboson Freeman said Gilead does not have to bear the costs incurred as a result of the defense.
Merck is trying to catch up with Gilead, which dominates the market for a new generation of hepatitis C drugs. Gillard’s drugs can cure more than 90 percent of people with hepatitis.
The case dates back as early as 2013, when Gilead and Merck suing each other against each other, both claiming to be the active ingredient in Gilead’s drug, the owner of Sofibbwe’s laboratory work.
U.S.-backed forces have announced that they have recaptured Manbij from the Islamic State.
A force spokesman said on Friday that all remaining Islamic State soldiers in the city had left and that U.S.-backed forces had taken full control of the northern city of Manbij, near the Turkish border.
The Syrian Democratic Forces (SDF) is now sweeping the city after the militants who hid in the city left.
Sharan Darwish of the Syrian Democratic Union's Manbij Military Council told Reuters that they had rescued more than 2,000 civilians who had been abducted by militants.
He told Reuters: "Manbij is now all under our control, but we're still carrying out a sweep."
The Clintons earned $10.75 million in 2015 and paid 34.2 percent in federal taxes.
Hillary Clinton released her 2105-year-old tax returns on Friday that showed the Democratic presidential candidate and her husband earned $10.75 million in 2015 and paid 34.2 percent in federal taxes.
In 2015, the Clintons made $1 million in philanthropic donations, most of which went to the Clinton Foundation; former President Bill Clinton’s speaking fee reached nearly $5.3 million, while the former secretary of state earned $3 million from publishers Simon & Schuster with a book about her tenure at the State Department.
Clinton’s running mate, Senator Tim Kaine of the United States of Virginia, and his wife, Anne Holden, released a 10-year-old tax return.
They paid a 20.3 percent federal tax in 2015.
Jennifer Palmieri, Clinton’s campaign aide, said in a statement: “Hillary Clinton and Tim Kaine will continue to serve as benchmarks for financial transparency.”
In stark contrast, Donald Trump glossed over and retracted his previous promise to release his tax returns on false grounds.
Although not required by law, U.S. presidential candidates should disclose their tax returns.
As a New York-based businessman, Trump and his lawyers cited IRS audits as a justification for refusing to release their tax returns.
Bill Clinton campaign aide Ian Sams said on Twitter that it was up to you and attached a link to the Democratic candidate’s tax returns.
Trump’s special counsel, Michael Cohen, told CNN on Thursday that he would not allow Trump to release his tax returns until the audit is complete.
Criticists, including 2012 Republican presidential nominee Mitt Romney and other Republicans, said Trump’s refusal to release his tax returns raised questions about his net worth, charitable donations, business dealings and various other relationships, including with Russia.
Ms. Clinton lashed out at the issue, releasing an online video on Friday in which high-profile Democrats urged Trump to disclose his tax status.
On Thursday, she raised the issue in an economic-policy speech in Michigan.
“For decades, he refused to publish his tax returns like other presidential candidates,” she said.
According to Politico, Mr. Trump paid virtually a penny in taxes in the 1990’s for two years in the 1990’s, and a New York Times business column on Friday cited a number of tax lawyers and accountants, all of whom said the current situation may still be the case.
The federal tax has become a major problem in the presidential race.
Mr. Mrs. Clinton named after a billionaire investor, Warren Buffet, a pledge to pay at least 30 per cent in taxes for people with an annual income of more than $1 million.
President Obama also supported the proposal.
Last week, Clinton held a rally in Omaha, Nebraska, where Mr. Buffett asked Mr. Trump to meet and exchange tax returns.
Buffett said that he is also being audited by the IRS and that what Trump is “afraid of” is not the tax authorities, but the voters.
The earliest tax returns published by the Clinton campaign were in 2007.
The Clintons, who currently live in Chabach, New York, paid an average federal rate of about 32% between 2007 and 2014, and a combined tax rate of about 40.5 percent.
The Clintons’ 2015 tax returns show that, unlike most Americans, they earn as little as $100 on wages.
Their main investments are low-cost index mutual funds, and the Clintons have a dividend and interest income of $109,000.
Reporting by Kevin Trobau; editing by Jonathan Odyssey
Jewish Filmmaker Criticizes Berlin Hotel for Deleting Israeli Phone Code as 'required' by Arab Customer - Reuters News
A French filmmaker of Jewish descent told the media that the Kempinski Hotel in Berlin did not list Israeli phone codes, and hotel employees said that this was in accordance with the "requirements" of Arab customers, which triggered an uproar in public opinion.
Claude Runzmann, author of the Holocaust documentary Shoah, expressed his disillusionment at the Kempinski Hotel and published an open letter in the German Frankfurter Allgemeine Zeitung.
During your recent stay, Longzman wanted to find Israel on the hotel's list of phone codes.
But Israel is not among the countries where guests can call directly from the room.
In 2016, the capital of Germany disappeared from Berlin.
Rontzmann wrote.
Instead, guests can call Israel through the Kempinski hotel’s call center.
Seeking an explanation, the filmmaker inquired at the hotel’s front desk.
In the letter, Longzman said he was “appalled” by the answers he received at the front desk.
Hotel staff said it was “a deliberate decision made by Kempinski hotel management.”
The reason for doing this made the filmmaker even more angry.
“Most of our guests were Arabs, and they demanded the removal of the Israeli code.”
Israel’s ambassador to Germany, Yakov Hadas Handelsmann, described the incident as a “humiliating disgrace.”
We were surprised to learn of the incident.
That in itself is a great shame.
It’s even more humiliating in Germany and the hotel chain.
There is no need for any explanation.
“We hope that the hotel can come to the right conclusion,” the official said.
The incident sparked a heated debate on the Internet, and everyone thought it was a scandal.
It is thought that the Kempinski Hotel is simply “chelling” to meet the demands of Arab customers.
Another post pointed directly to the hotel's "disgraceful", and pointed out that the street, located on the famous Kudham Street, was located near a synagogue.
According to Der Spiegel, the hotel quickly clarified all the allegations, claiming that everything was “negligent” and “apologised” to Longzeman.
Kempinski was quoted as saying: “There has never been a direct order to remove Israel from the fast dial list.”
The newspaper also said that the Israeli code had been added to the list.
Police use tear gas and rubber bullets to deplete protesting Brazilian students
In Sao Paulo, Brazil, on Thursday, students clashed with the police as they were protesting reforms in the government’s public education system.
Police used tear gas and rubber bullets to deport the protesters.
Law enforcement officials tried to disperse the students, so the police used rubber bullets and tear gas.
Hundreds of students participated in the march to express their displeasure with these programs.
In order to save money, the governor of the State of Sao Paulo Orkmin plans to shut down 100 public schools, and 300,000 students will be transferred.
Some of the students who participated in the protest expressed their displeasure with interim President Michelle Temer through graffiti on the walls.
Just a few days before the most recent protest, protesters collectively took to the streets in support of President Dilma Rousseff, who was impeached by the country’s Senate.
Scottish cyclist Calm Scandiner returned after winning the cycling gold medal.
Scottish cyclist Carm Skinner last night at the men’s team race at the Rio Cycling venue helped the British trio to successfully defend their Olympic gold medal after the 2012 London Olympics.
The 23-year-old Glasgow cyclist replaced his fellow Scot, Sir Chris Hoy, as the centre of the team. Even the storied cyclist was proud when the young Sjinner returned from defeating the favourite New Zealand.
Four years ago, the British team made an astounding, and Hoy won the fifth of six individual Olympic gold medals.
The United Kingdom finished only sixth at the World Cycling Fields Championships in London in March, and Hoy has retired since then. The British team then made another brilliance.
Between the Beijing Olympics and the London Olympics, Britain’s team’s problem was replacing “first-in-a-thirsty” Jamie Stuff.
The team did just that when Sinders showed up.
Hoy’s decommissioning also leaves a void, and Chein Imadi and Matt Krampton both want to fill the void.
After seeing Steiner's potential, the British men's coaching staff insisted that he be included in the national team, and Sjinner eventually met the expectations.
Skinner was paired by Sindez and Kenny, who won the gold medal with Hoy four years ago. The trio set a new Olympic record in the qualifiers, but was overtaken by New Zealand in the first round.
And these three British bicycle races finally defeated their opponents and won the gold medal.
Although Hinds was a little behind, Kenny took the lead for the team, and Steiner maintained that lead to the end.
A change in strategy was the key to this reversal, with Sinders opting for the larger flywheel, which was slower, which allowed Kenny, and Skinner in particular, to maintain its speed.
Hoy watched the match as a BBC commentator. Steiner, Kenny, and Sinders saw him on the podium.
Sjinner, a 23-year-old Glasgow cyclist, said: "It flatters me."
I’m just doing everything I can to make myself famous.
We set an Olympic record in the final and defeated the world champion.
It's unbelievable.
There is nothing better than this victory.
After winning gold medals with Kenny and Hoy at the 2012 London Olympics, Sindez admitted to deliberately falling on the track with a poor start.
Later, he retracted the comment, and the opponents of the British team could not appeal.
There are no such problems in this victory.
“It’s like in London, the British flag on the platform.”
We were just teamed up three months ago.
“We’ve lost a lot of world championships, so it’s amazing to be able to defend an Olympic champion.
This is only a competition and a gold medal for the British team that won seven of the 10 venue cycling gold medals at the Beijing Olympic Games and the London Olympic Games.
“If this symbolizes the progress we’ve made over the past five months, we’re going to continue our success over the next five days.”
Depending on Kenny’s performance, it’s not impossible for him to reproduce Hoy’s feat of winning three gold medals at an Olympic Games.
If that’s the case, he’s 12 years younger than Hoy, and also on March 23 (which seems to be a sacred day for British sport, Steve Redgrave, Mo Farah and Roger Bannister were also born on that day), Kenny, who will have six gold medals and a silver medal.
This achievement is the same as that of Hoyton.
Kenny will compete in a three-day race that begins today.
The 28-year-on-year-old said: “I’m going to focus on the game for the time being.
Team racing is always the best.
You can win the game with your teammates.
To put it bluntly, it’s a little lonely for a person to win.
Hinds said: "If he can win the other two gold medals, then he will be awarded the knighthood."
It’s the only game of the day to produce a medal, but the British team received other good news.
Sir Bradley Wiggins, Ed Clancy, Steven Bourke and Owen Douer advanced to the four-man four-kilometre team pursuit with the fastest result.
Their score was 351.943.
The gold medalist at the London 2012 Olympic Games has a world record of 351.659.
In the first and final (10:42 p.m.), Wiggins will no doubt be in the spotlight.
He got into an altercation with tournament officials ahead of qualifiers yesterday, when tournament officials asked him to measure his height.
In the women’s group competition, which will end tomorrow, Laura Trotter, Joanna Rossel Chand, Eleanor Barker and Kate Archibald from Milguet advanced with a new world record of 413.260.
The British team relies on its strong venue cycling team to occupy the initiative in the middle of the Olympic Games and won a number of medals.
After showing its absolute dominance at the Beijing and London Olympics, the British Cycling team was a little disappointed when it went to Rio.
There have been a number of twists and turns, including April’s technical superintendent Sean Sutton resigned over allegations of sexism and bullying and the decommissioning of legends such as Hoy and Victoria Pendleton.
But Cycling Hall's first race night is enough to prove that the British team will once again stage the legend of reaching the pinnacle at a critical moment.
After small life comes into this world, parents are responsible for this life, this responsibility lies not only in the child's physical health, but also in spiritual development, that is, education.
If the child's education fails, then even if the career is successful, it will not be able to make up for the shortcomings of life and the failure of the family.
When a new life arrives, the new parents will take the time and effort to take care of and educate the children and take responsibility for him.
Responsibilities, in addition to being reflected in the protection of the body and making them healthy, also lies in spiritual education, that is, allowing children to learn how to be human, how to be adults, and how to succeed.
Good family education means that parents often need to accompany their children, give their children care and patient care, and also need to teach their children to develop civilized words and deeds, so that children can better learn knowledge and improve their intelligence.
The words and deeds of parents will affect the child's growth, they will imitate their own parents, that is, it is often said that dragons and dragons, phoenix and phoenix, rat's son will hit a hole, what kind of children the parents.
Therefore, parents in front of their children need to be a good role model, standardize their own words and deeds, and cultivate their own excellent character, which can indirectly help the child to build a good heart and make him better.
Amy is a smart and pretty girl.
She is outgoing and lively, can get along well with her friends, and has a good ability to adapt to the environment.
However, Amy has a little secret: she can’t focus on the studies and tasks she’s going to do for a long time.
It's been a secret with Amy for a long time. It doesn't have a serious problem.
Even through the decentralized, modular time to learn and work, she can basically complete the task and achieve good results.
However, when the task is heavy and the time is tight, Amy feels a lot of pain and torture.
An individual’s resistance to self-exposure and its emotional experience is intended not to put an individual’s self-knowledge and self-esteem at risk.
There are also behaviorist psychologists who understand impedance as an individual’s disobedience to their behavior.
I tried to get Amy to do an exercise to calm herself through the way she breathed and felt the pain.
As soon as she got out of the trapped situation, she felt relaxed and regained her freedom.
The 63-year-old vagabond, Han, had an argument with another vagabond Xiao after drinking, and then strangled him with a knife.
Han said that before the incident, he and the vagabond Xiao both lived on the ground in an alley in the eastern city, and the two were more than 20 meters apart.
Han said that on the same day of the incident, they were called by their friends to drink together, and the two had two quarrels during and after dinner.
Han said that he was afraid that Xiao would beat him, so he picked up a fruit knife from the garbage pile and killed him.
In the court, the victim's family demanded more than 530,000 yuan in compensation for funeral expenses and death compensation.
Uber's entry into the Taiwan market for four years has had a considerable impact on the local traditional taxi industry.
Taiwan's "United Daily News" reported on August 12 that on the morning of the 12th, more than 100 taxis bypassed Taiwan's "administrative court" in protest, resulting in serious traffic paralysis in the surrounding area.
Zheng Lijia, chairman of the Taipei City Drivers' Trade Union, said that Uber came to Taiwan for four years, the Taiwan authorities only held a meeting at the end of this month, and the drivers can no longer wait.
However, there is no trust in the government, which is delayed again and again.
Law-abiding taxi drivers belonging to low-level workers feel cheated by the authorities by competing with illegal but unfettered Uber.
Original title: 2,000 chickens in a farm in Jiangsu were sentenced by the court's unauthorized sale
After the judgment came into effect, because Li did not automatically fulfill the obligations determined by the judgment, Wang applied to the Shuyang court for enforcement.
On October 16, 2014, the Shuyang court issued a civil ruling, ruling that 2,000 laying hens on all of Li's farms should be detained, and they could not be transferred or sold without permission.
After receiving the seizure decision, Li privately sold some of the laid hens impounded in the farm without the permission of the Shuyang court.
As of March 8, 2015, the Shuyang County Public Security Bureau surveyed, there were only 142 laying hens in the farm.
The reporter learned on August 12 that the Beijing 2022 Winter Olympic and Paralympic Organizing Committee issued an announcement that the Beijing Winter Olympic Organizing Committee inherited intellectual property rights such as the emblem and logo of the Beijing Winter Olympic Application Committee.
Without the permission of the Beijing Winter Olympic Organizing Committee, no one may use the emblem and logo of the Beijing Winter Olympic Committee for commercial purposes.
The head of the industrial coordination department of the National Development and Reform Commission pointed out here today that steel overcapacity is a global problem.
In recent years, China's capacity utilization rate has been higher than the global average, and it is also higher than the United States, Europe and other countries and regions.
Our country has taken resolute and effective measures to defuse excess capacity, and the results are gradually emerging.
The person in charge pointed out that on the global problem of steel overcapacity, the Party Central Committee and the State Council attach great importance to it.
All departments and regions have actively implemented the deployment of the State Council and worked earnestly to reduce the crude steel production capacity of about 45 million tons this year.
Starting from China's national conditions, our country does not encourage steel exports, on the contrary, it also takes a series of practical measures to control steel exports.
The person in charge stressed that the international trade of steel products is essentially a market behavior, which is an independent choice after considering factors such as the needs of the importing country and consumers considering the cost performance of the products.
The implementation of trade protection measures will not help to fundamentally solve the development problems of the global steel industry; on the contrary, it will only have a further impact on the international trade order.
When it comes to debt, the person in charge stressed that resolving the debt problem is an important issue that needs to be properly handled in the process of resolving excess capacity.
Due to the large-scale and wide-ranging assets of iron and steel enterprises, the debt relationship of some enterprises is complex, and if it is improperly disposed of, it is likely to cause regional risks.
According to the person in charge, in recent years, with the increasing downward pressure on the economy, the total social demand has gradually weakened, the capacity utilization rate of some industries has declined, and the production and operation difficulties of enterprises have increased.
Some enterprises do not adapt to the changes in the market environment, production and operation are unsustainable or even on the verge of bankruptcy, but subject to some institutional and institutional factors, there are more obstacles to exit in a market-oriented way, becoming "zombie enterprises".
The existence of such enterprises has distorted market signals, reduced the efficiency of factor resource utilization, increased the cost of social management, and hindered the establishment of a fair competition market environment.
The main reason for the losses is the same as the difficulties faced by the global steel industry - sluggish market demand and low capacity utilization.
China mainly adopts market mechanisms, economic means and the rule of law methods, and the government is mainly to do a good job for employees and social stability to ensure a fair and just market order.
The person in charge stressed that in the next step, we must unswervingly continue to do a good job in the production capacity to ensure the completion of the target task of resolving crude steel production capacity of 100 million to 150 million tons in five years.
On the afternoon of the 10th, as soon as China's tourist police appeared in Moscow's Red Square, it immediately attracted people's attention, and Chinese tourists waved with surprise, and locals and foreign tourists couldn't help but look back.
On the same day, China's first professional tourist police team, members of the tourist police detachment of Sanya Public Security Bureau in Hainan Province, came to Moscow's Red Square to exchange and study with the local tourist police on duty.
The Moscow tourist police were divided into three small groups in Red Square, Nikolinsky Pedestrian Street, Güm department store and other places, and the Chinese tourism police studied together, and the whole process lasted for more than an hour.
Liusine, a female police officer in her 20s who speaks both English and Spanish, joined the tourist police force last year.
Along the way, he took a closer look at the words and deeds of his Russian counterparts and communicated with her from time to time.
When the Spanish tourists came to consult, the Moscow tourist police patiently explained each other in fluent Spanish, which impressed Wang Bing.
“Everyone in the Moscow tourist police speaks a foreign language, and there will be more than two, which is very touching to us.”
"Hainan, as an international tourism island, is gradually attaching importance to attracting international tourists, and we hope to improve our ability to match the status of international tourism islands."
On the same day, the Chinese tourism police also went to the Moscow city tourism police brigade to communicate with their Russian counterparts.
“I’ve always dealt with Chinese tourists and it’s great to see them visiting Russia.”
“The question they usually ask for help is how the road goes, where a monument is located, how to rent, how to get back to the hotel.”
Resakov, captain of the Moscow City Tourism Police Brigade, said that in recent years, the city's urban environment and tourist atmosphere have become more and more attractive to foreign tourists.
In order to meet the needs of the development of tourism, a tourism police team was set up in July 2014, which is responsible for patrolling and guarding major scenic spots to help and guide tourists.
At present, all Moscow tourist police officers are proficient in English, and some also speak Spanish and German.
According to their foreign language level, the police brigade divided them into nine groups and took classes twice a week to learn self-defense methods, laws and regulations and foreign languages.
"There are currently two tourist police officers who have begun to learn Chinese and have spoken well, and we will continue to improve their Chinese language level," Resakov said.
Resakov told reporters that the Moscow tourism police have accumulated a certain amount of experience since its formation, hoping to enlighten their Sanya counterparts.
He believes that the cooperation between the police departments of Russia and China will enhance the safety of their own citizens to travel to each other's countries.
“Moscow tourist police personnel recruitment, police mode, equipment and good interaction with tourists have given us a lot of inspiration,” Chen Xiaokun said.
At present, Hebei, Jilin, Tianjin, Jiangxi, Sichuan, Hainan, Gansu, Fujian, Beijing and other nine provinces and cities have issued residence permit implementation rules.
With regard to the conditions for applying for a residence permit, it is generally proposed in the above-mentioned areas to live for more than half a year, which meets one of the conditions for legal and stable employment, legal and stable residence and continuous education.
In terms of the treatment provided by the residence permit, the "gold content" in various places is different, and the scope of public services and facilities provided in some areas has been expanded compared with the provisions of the national version.
In these areas, it is easier for children to participate in the secondary and high school entrance examination if they meet the relevant conditions.
In addition, Beijing and many other places have also made clear requirements to gradually expand the provision of public services and facilities, and regularly announced them to the public.
For example, Fujian put forward that the scope of public services and facilities enjoyed by residence permit holders should be announced to the public at least once every three years.
The "Provisional Regulations on Residency Certificates" stipulates that if they meet the conditions for the handling of the residence permit, the public security organ shall, within 15 days from the date of acceptance, produce and issue a residence permit.
With regard to the time limit for the issuance of certificates, most of them are in agreement with the national version, that is, they will be issued within 15 days.
Hebei made it clear that for those who meet the application conditions and have complete materials, the public security police station in the place of residence should issue a residence permit within 3 working days from the date of acceptance.
In accordance with Jiangxi's regulations, in order to meet the conditions for applying for a residence permit and the certification materials are complete, the public security organ shall produce and issue a residence permit within 5 working days from the date of acceptance.
In accordance with the provisions of the "Regulations on Residency Certificates", the above-mentioned areas have made it clear that they apply for a residence permit for the first time and are exempted.
For example, Sichuan requires local public security police stations or entrusted community service institutions to strictly implement the approved charging items and charging standards, and resolutely prohibit excessive, excessive fees or taxi charges.
After investigation, on July 27, 2016, Chen Yangxia, the former secretary of the Dingnan County Party Committee of Ganzhou City, went to the provincial discipline commission to report to work and served as the director of the party's style and political style supervision office (deputy director-level with a probation period of one year).
The red wine he drank that night was provided by Li Youcai personally, and the other expenses were borne by someone in Liu.
The Jiangxi Provincial Disciplinary Commission reported that Chen Yangxia, Cheng Ziliang and others organized and accepted food invitations in private clubhouses, in violation of the spirit of the eight provisions of the Central Committee and violated the discipline of the party.
Pogba, who received two yellow cards in the Italian Cup last season, will be automatically suspended for one match according to the rules.
Although he has transferred back to the Premier League, the FA still extended its cumulative suspension to the Premier League stage.
As a result of this, in the away game against Bournemouth on August 14, Pogba will be on the wall, and his return to Manchester United's debut will be postponed to the 20th home game with Southampton.
As the No. 12 rookie in the first round in 2014, Sarici will officially land in the NBA next season and join the Philadelphia 76ers.
As a young European player, many fans did not know him very well, but through this Olympic Games, I believe that Saariq's performance has left a deep impression.
The last time Croatia narrowly defeated Spain, Sarić successfully capped Paul Gasol at the last minute and tried to drag the game into an extended basket.
In recent days, 76ers coach Brett Brown gave Sarics a very high rating, and the Spurs manager believes that he has seen the shadow of the young Manu Ginobili in Sarics.
It’s been clear that Sarics has shown his talent and left the 76ers looking forward to him.
In Croatia's first two games at the Olympic Games, Sarici had a total of 24 points, 17 rebounds and 12 assists.
In the first half, Sarici showed his ability to open the space on the field, and after blocking with his teammates, he was able to shoot outside the three-point line.
Although the 76ers are currently hoarding a number of talented young players, they do not have Sarich's outside ability.
From the cover to the launch of a long-range attack and complete the assists, there are only a handful of inner players who can do this in the NBA game today.
Since the beginning of the Olympic Games, Sarich has averaged 13 points, 8 rebounds and 5 assists in three games.
Since his decision to return to the Cavaliers in the summer of 2014, James has signed two consecutive 1+1 contracts.
As the NBA’s collective bargaining agreement enters its final year, as the vice president of the NBA’s players’ union, James will be at the forefront of collective agreement negotiations.
In view of the sharp increase in the league's revenue, thanks to the new TV broadcast agreement, as well as the battle between owners and players on how to deal with the money, there are fears that the NBA will fall into a shutdown next summer.
But for James, he doesn’t have to worry about becoming a free agent next summer because he’s already extended a three-year contract with the Cavaliers.
No matter when the 2017-18 season officially begins, James is under the contract.
Since the amazing appearance of the iPhone SE, the mobile phone market has also ushered in the boom of small screen machines.
Not long ago, Nubia also launched the first work of its Z11 series: nubiaZ11mini.
The nubiaZ11mini continues with its excellent photography genes, and is equipped with a 5.0-inch screen that is easier to hold with a single-handed and easy-to-use rear fingerprint recognition, resulting in an outstanding experience.
Nubia has just listed a small-screen camera mobile phone Z11mini price reduction of 200 yuan, that is, from the original 1499 yuan down to 1299 yuan.
In terms of appearance, the nubiaZ11mini adopts a 5-inch 1080P screen, which is still the classic "little red circle" design at the bottom.
The middle frame is made of metallic material, with a symmetrical design at the bottom with a Type-C data interface.
The future of the Portland smelter is fraught with uncertainty due to the cancellation of a power supply contract.
Because the power company that powers the plant has revealed that a factory owner will terminate a supply contract that invalidates all supply contracts, the Portland aluminum smelter in Victoria and hundreds of factory workers are currently facing an uncertain future.
The move comes after the Victorian government’s decision not to proceed with subsidised guaranteed plant operations.
The 20-year fixed subsidy will end in November.
2,000 workers at Alcoa’s Portland plant could face job losses.
Once the factory closes, as many as 2,000 people may lose their jobs directly or indirectly.
And because the plant accounts for about 10 percent of Victoria’s total electricity output, it may also have a ripple effect.
In 2014, Al Aluminium shut down its Cape Hanry smelter, which led to the closure of the Anglesey Island power plant last year.
Alcoa’s Portland smelter is currently losing money and is at risk of closure.
The move comes after the factory’s forecast for the next few years, initially due to the strength of the Australian dollar and, more recently, because of the price of the plant’s products.
AGL supplies electricity to this large aluminum smelter through the La Trobe Valley Old Eyang power plant. The company predicts that three other plant owners will also terminate its agreement.
The factory’s largest shareholder is a joint venture between Aluminium and Alumina, while China’s CITIC Group and Japan’s Marubeni also hold a small stake.
“AGL expects the Portland plant to continue to operate, which means that the smelter will continue to generate demand for electricity,” the joint venture said.
AGL said the contracts were “hedging contracts” that should have come into effect since November 2016.
The contracts will be terminated for a period of 12 months, so they will be terminated in 2017.
“As a result, AGL still forecasts that these contracts will continue to generate revenue in fiscal year 2017.”
Any revenue impact on AGL from fiscal year 2018 is currently subject to an upbeat outlook for wholesale electricity prices in futures markets.
AGL said it has written down $187 million of the contract value in “expectations for termination activities.”
Al Aluminium said that its decision to terminate these contracts “does not affect Aluminium’s ability to operate the smelter or guarantee its power supply.”
The U.S. company said it had signed a 20-year contract in 2010 that was supposed to go into effect in November, but the company did not explain why it withdrew from the contract.
Analysts are cautious about whether the Portland smelter in Victoria and the Tomargo plant near Newcastle will be closed because of the industry’s poor economic situation.
In response to analysts’ comments earlier this week, AGL’s head of operations, Steven Mickelson, said Portland consumes about 600 megawatts of electricity per year and the Tomargo plant reaches about 900 megawatts per year.
If the two factories are closed, the demand in the electricity market will be greatly reduced.
“As an electric company, that’s not good news for us.”
A community law center keeps 160,000 people out every year.
More than 160,000 of the most underprivileged groups are shut out by community law centres each year. Funding for the service is already overstretched and is now facing further funding cuts.
In Queensland, three out of every five people are turned away when seeking free legal advice and representation, most of them elderly, migrants, vulnerable workers, victims of violence and those who do not have the resources to fight unjust evictions.
The lack of funding for community-based legal services has already exceeded the limit and now faces further funding cuts.
Starting in June next year, the federal government’s funding of these legal centers will be reduced by another 30 percent.
James Farrell, head of the Queensland Community Law Centre, said thousands of people were turned away every year, according to the latest National Community Association Legal Centre survey.
Mr Farrell said it would only get worse if the federal government doesn’t change its existing decisions.
He said: “Queen Queensland’s community law centres are chronically underfunded, which means thousands of people will not have access to the vital services they need.”
People who need to stay away from violence, people with huge debts that can’t be repaid, families who face disintegrated families, workers who are being squeezed, are facing legal problems, and the report shows that they don’t get the help they need.
The federal government will cut funding by an additional 30 per cent from June 2017, which means that thousands of vulnerable people in Queensland will be forced to face complex legal problems without help.
“We call on George Brandis, Minister of Justice and Queensland MP, to rescind these funding cuts immediately so that people can get the help they need in the face of legal issues.
Last year, the state government pledged to raise legal aid funding to the national average.
It is time to pay attention to community law centres and their response to the needs of the community, and the government must also invest in this important work.
The Donald Trump campaign has been indicted for pulling a gun.
NEW YORK (AP) — Trump’s campaign has been sued for inaction by the head of Northern California for pulling a gun at a staff member while driving a jeep in February.
Vincent Bodini, the state's campaign's former software trainer, described the incident on Wednesday in a Charlotte-based state court.
Bodini said he had hoped the matter could be resolved internally, but after waiting for several months he realized that “it couldn’t happen.”
According to Bodini's description, the person in charge, Earl Phillips, "pulled out a pistol, put his right index finger on the board, and aimed the muzzle at Vincent's kneecap."
After filing a complaint with local and regional campaign leadership, Bodini learned that at least four other people were experiencing the same thing.
Bodini said in the complaint: “The absence of a shot does not mean that there will be no harm.”
Just two days before the case, the Republican presidential candidate in North Carolina told the crowd in North Carolina that if his opponent Hillary Clinton is elected and picks the judge she loves, the “supporters of the Second Amendment,” that is, gun owners and gun enthusiasts, are likely to take action.
Trump’s campaign said the media took his words out of context and that he did not advocate violence.
In his complaint, Bodini demanded compensation from the campaign’s team for his neglitter supervision, as well as Philip for his attacks, beatings, and mental injuries.
Trump’s spokesman, Hope Hicks, did not immediately respond to the news.
I couldn’t get in touch with Philip.
According to WCCB, a local news agency in Charlotte, Phillips recently left the campaign team.
His consulting firm Innovative Consulting Services did not immediately respond to calls.
Republican presidential candidate Donald Trump’s campaign is controversial.
In this case, Bodini competes with President Donald Trump, 16-CS-14300, the U.S. Superior Court of Mecklenburg Prefecture (Charlotte).
The United Kingdom must transmit the Olympic spirit and carry out an expansion of Heathrow Airport
Heathrow will also bring vitality and prosperity to our communities, London and the country as a whole.
“For me, that’s where Heathrow’s fascination, as at the 2012 London Olympics, we did our best to ensure that our country and region could benefit from these events.
The Olympics have greatly benefited Strattford and the Eastern District.
“We will once again benefit the region by creating opportunities for local people and businesses near Heathrow.”
In terms of our local communities alone, we will create 10,000 new apprenticeships, 40,000 new jobs, and lift the number of young people around the airport out of unemployment.
Just as before the London Olympics in 2012, some people thought that Heathrow’s expansion project was too large.
“I’ve been told that Britain won’t be ready for the Olympics and that we’re humiliating in front of the whole world.
The skeptics’ skepticism about the 2012 Olympics is wrong, and their skepticism about the Heathrow project will also prove wrong.
Although there will always be obstacles that need to be overcome, Heathrow is solving every problem.
Like the Olympic Games, Heathrow is an infrastructure project for the majority, not the minority.
The expansion will create as many as 180,000 new jobs, generate £21 billion in economic growth, and leave a wealth of technology and jobs around the airport and across the UK.
We have an excellent Heathrow project team. The team has completed an infrastructure investment project of £11 billion on time and on budget, including Terminal T5, which has been named the world's best airport terminal for five consecutive years and the T2 terminal located between the world's two busiest runways.
Now, they are ready to build a third runway with a private investment of £16 billion.
The United Kingdom successfully hosted the London 2012 Olympic Games, and I am confident that the Heathrow expansion project will also be very successful.
It’s a good time for us to convey the Olympic spirit and expand Heathrow, so that we can protect our future and create a wealth of technology and jobs that the United Kingdom is proud.
Lord Paul Dayton is Chairman of the Board of Heathrow and a former Commercial Counsellor at the UK Treasury.
A woman commits suicide on a Swiss freeway has been killed.
The victims were lying on the highway at midnight.
The woman, who tried to kill herself, was pulled over by several cars on the highway early Thursday morning. Police are currently searching for witnesses.
The accident occurred on the A1 motorway near Morges, Wa state, in the early hours of Thursday morning.
War County police said a woman was lying “desperately” in the middle of the night on the road and had been squashed by multiple vehicles.
The victim, a 49-year-old Swiss woman, was acting with apparent suicidal intent. She had been squashed by several vehicles, including a van.
The woman died instantly.
Police revealed that several of the drivers involved have been investigated, but some drivers have still not been identified. Police are calling on them, as well as witnesses of the accident, to come to the investigation.
Guilles Hofstadter's lawyer told the Geneva Tribune that a criminal investigation has now begun, which is a routine process for such incidents.
However, it has not yet been known whether the driver will face the charges.
Is it possible to avoid colliding?
Hofstadter said: "This will be determined by the prosecutor."
Depending on the outcome of two other similar cases over the past five years, the driver will not be liable.
According to the newspaper, both cases were caused by people walking on the highway late at night. The final verdict was that the driver could not have predicted that pedestrians would cross the highway at midnight.
Last year, a police officer was accused of negligently causing the death of a man in August 2014 when she rammed a man on the A1 freeway near Payenne and killed him.
The 22-year-old victim crossed the road after drinking.
After the investigation, the judge said that the female police officer's driving behavior at that time was completely legal, that the man's appearance on the road was "completely unexpected and unpredictable", and that the female police officer later made an emergency call.
Anyone who can provide information about this incident near Mouri on Thursday should contact the police at 021 644 83 46 or 021 644 44 44.
NASA's climate model was once suitable for human habitation on Venus
According to NASA's new climate model, Venus used to be suitable for human habitation.
Scientists at NASA’s Goddard Institute for Space Research have developed a model that can explore the past of Venus, using tools and algorithms that are very similar to those used by climate scientists.
The model is used to determine whether Venus, whose surface is hot, water-free and whose atmosphere is filled with carbon dioxide, once had an Earth-like environment.
Previously, scientists believed that the rotation rate of Venus was slower because of its thicker atmosphere.
But the latest simulations suggest that Venus may once have had a thinner, Earth-like atmosphere and at the same slower rotation rate at the time.
The model can also show the early topography of Venus.
Venus is likely to have more dry areas than Earth, but there used to be enough water and geographical changes to nurture life and prevent rapid evaporation.
In the early days, the sunlight shining on Venus was 30% brighter than Earth’s.
Anthony del Geno, a scientist at the Goddard Space Research Institute, explained at a press conference: “In the model simulation of the Goddard Space Research Institute, the slow rotation of Venus makes the daytime on its side for nearly two months.”
This warms the surface and produces rainwater capable of forming thick clouds, which, like an umbrella, blocks most of the sun’s heat from the ground.
As a result of the simulation, the average climate temperature of Venus is actually a few degrees lower than the current Earth.
The evolution of Venus simulated in this model is similar to that previously predicted by planetary scientists.
Although there may have been life on Venus, over the course of billions of years, Venus has been exposed to excessive temperatures and ultraviolet rays.
The ocean on the planet evaporates, and the water vapor is also consumed by ultraviolet light.
With the escape of hydrogen, only a thicker atmosphere of carbon dioxide and a deadly greenhouse-gaseous effect were left, resulting in Venus as we know it today.
The researchers published simulations of a new Venusian climate model in the journal Geophysical Research Communications.
Patrick Roy resigns as avalanche coach
Patrick Roy, who resigned as head coach and vice president of the Colorado avalanche ice hockey team on Thursday, said he had no say at the team’s decision-making level.
Colorado executive vice-command Joe Saatsis confirmed the news and said the club would immediately start looking for a new head coach.
The 50-year-old Roy said in a statement: "Over the past three years, I've fulfilled my responsibilities as head coach and vice president of the Colorado Avalanche with energy, passion and determination."
“Throughout the summer, I’ve been thinking hard about how I can improve this team to the next level.
To this end, the goals of the head coach and the vice president must be in line with the goals of the club.
He must also have a say in the decisions that affect the team’s performance.
However, at present, these conditions have not yet been fulfilled.
Sarkis hired Roy on May 23, 2013, and he thanked Roy for his contributions to the team.
"Patrick told me about his decision today."
“We thank him for his contribution to the club and look forward to his success in the future.”
Roe was nominated for the Jack Adams Award for Best Coach of the league in his first season in 2013-14 for the avalanche team.
He helped the club with 112 points, ranking first in the Central Division. However, the Colorado team was eliminated by the Minnesota team in the first round of the playoffs and missed the playoffs in the past two years.
In the 2015-16 season, the avalanche team's results were 39 wins, 39 draws and 4 losses, and finally lost the second wild card qualification in the Western Major League region by 5 points.
As a Hall of Fame keeper, Roy has won a total of four Stanley Cups, winning two for the Montreal Canadiens and Avalanches.
North Sea oil field workers stop strike, continue negotiations
Chief Negotiators said workers at the North Sea oil fields had halted a strike on pay, and the parties to the dispute began a new round of negotiations.
There have been a number of strikes against oil-field service company Wood Group on the North Sea oil platform operated by Royal Dutch Shell.
According to a joint statement, “Wood Group, as well as the Unite and RMT unions, can confirm that we have agreed to reopen the current dispute settlement process.”
Starting early next week, we’ll have a number of full-day meetings in the coming weeks to re-examine these issues.
The union said its recent action was aimed at protesting a pay cut of up to 30 per cent, the first in 25 years.
The Wood Group this year has slashed North Sea contractor’s compensation by about 9 percent due to market pressures.
Prior to this salary cut, the company reduced the compensation of offshore contractors by 10 percent in 2014.
The company said that another pay cut will help the company through the market downturn.
Shell has laid off thousands of its staff and announced plans to shut down oil and gas equipment in 10 countries due to the company’s need to streamline its operations following a merger with British energy company British Gas.
Energy companies are coming under pressure from falling crude prices and Britain’s Brexit decision in June.
Dave Anderson, a member of Scotland’s parliament, met with union leaders earlier this week to discuss the biggest labour dispute in a generation in the North Sea.
He said that the North Sea is very important to the regional economy.
Dave said in a statement: “In the North Sea and the country as a whole, we need an economy that serves the many, not the few.”
Spending on new projects in the North Sea is not expected to exceed $1.4 billion in 2016, compared with about $7 billion in average project expenditure over the past five years.
Kepler measured the rotation velocity of the stars of the Angna Cluster
The Kepler space telescope’s latest mission has helped astronomers collect the most complete stellar rotation velocities.
The new data is helping astronomers understand why the cluster’s stars have different rotational velocities as well as the association between their orbital periods and the planet’s composition.
In a press release, Lusa Rebble, a research scientist at the Center for Infrared Processing Analysis at Caltech in Pasadena, said: "We hope to further understand the relationship between star mass, age, and even the history of its solar system by comparing our results with other star clusters."
It is located 445 light-years from Earth.
Many of the stars in this cluster were born about 125 million years ago and have just reached adulthood.
They achieve the highest rotation speed in a lifetime.
At their highest rotational velocity, these mature stars emit a large number of stellar winds.
When these stellar winds pass through the star’s magnetic field, they brake on the star.
As the age of the star increases, its rotation begins to slow down.
Kepler measured the rotational velocity of individual stars by tracking the time of the emergence of the identified stellar sunspots (such as sunspots).
The most recent velocity data set suggests that more massive stars rotate more slowly than lower-mass stars.
Rable compares stars to dancers, and larger dancers spin more slowly than smaller dancers.
“In the ballet performance of the Angsu cluster, we found that stars with slower rotations tend to be more massive, while the fastest stars tend to be the lightest.”
Due to the close proximity of Angsu clusters, it can be used as an ideal cosmic laboratory for comparing stellar mass and rotation velocities.
Rebble said: "The Angsu cluster lays the foundation for a theoretical model of bidirectional rotation of young and elderly stars."
There’s still a lot we need to know about how, when, and why stars slow down their rotations and “repench their dancing shoes.”
Rebble and her colleagues elaborated on their latest analysis of the rate of rotation of Ang Cesar clusters in three new essays. The three papers will soon be published in the Journal of Astronomy.
